                <string>PROSOCHE Capability Gate — spike 002.

Tests whether one shortcut can replace two forks (Dumb / Sentient) using a manual opt-in toggle plus an ordering-based fail-safe instead of hardware detection.

The design under test: the core deterministic escalation always runs FIRST and unconditionally. The optional on-device AI step runs LAST and only when the user opted in. If the AI step fails on hardware without Apple Intelligence, the shortcut halts there — but the core escalation has already completed. Shortcuts has no error-recovery branch, so ordering is the only available fail-safe.</string>
            </dict>
        </dict>

